      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The original test:\n1. Has many unused data provider methods (`data_badDates`, `data_badLeapDates`, `data_lengthOfMonth`, etc.)\n2. The `iso` (LocalDate) column in `data_samples` is never used in the test body\n3. Has dozens of unused imports\n4. Lacks a clear name/description explaining the test's intent\n\nI'll write an improved version that removes all unused code and adds clarity.Now I'll compile-check it.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version removes all unused data provider methods and irrelevant imports, simplifies `data_samples` to a single-column array of `Symmetry010Date` values (eliminating the unused `LocalDate iso` parameter), groups historical entries with descriptive comments, and adds a `@DisplayName` to clearly express the invariant being tested: *a date's period until itself is always zero*."
